Found under k16. With no GitHub and no Gitea remote the bundle adds [Repository], which reads only remote.<git_remote>.url (git_remote defaults to origin) and otherwise falls back to `git svn info` ("git: svn is not a git command" on stderr). k16 leaves [Repository] out when there is no remote at all; a repository whose only remote is e.g. upstream still gets [Repository] and the noise, and no resources.repository. Possible shape: pass git_remote => the name of the first remote from _remote_urls() (origin first). Behaviour change for such dists (they would gain resources.repository), so a decision, not a silent fix.

2026-11-09 20:45 Fix form (branch k22-k25, uncommitted yet): new lazy _remote_name = the first entry of _remote_urls() (origin first), the same remote _remote_host describes. In the _has_remote branch of configure(), [Repository] gets git_remote => that name only when it is not origin; with origin the plugin config is exactly as before (no argument). Verified: only an upstream on gitlab -> resources.repository with type/url/web, stderr empty (main: svn noise and empty hashes); github origin -> byte-identical to main. Same gap in GiteaMeta and GithubMeta (read only remote.origin.url) filed as k26.

2026-11-09 21:23 Tests (uncommitted): t/repository_remote.t +14: _remote_name (origin wins even when listed later; without origin the first remote in config order; undef without remote / without .git, forced inside the tempdir); plugin list: only upstream -> Repository {git_remote=>'upstream'}, several without origin -> the first, gitlab origin / origin+upstream / github origin with no_github=1 -> Repository without payload, no remote -> no Repository. t/support_build.t: full build with only a gitlab upstream -> resources.repository with type/url/web, no svn on STDERR. Counter-check against main: the new upstream/first-remote asserts red, the origin/no-remote ones green.

